+unique on its own; a clause carries no `anchor:`, `evidence:`, or `links:`
+of its own — it is a decomposition of its parent's single `text`, not a
+new object kind, and inherits the parent's evidence expectations and body
+anchor. `clauses:` is optional and `omitempty`: an object with three or
+fewer claims (§Lint rules' under-enumeration threshold) is never required
+to add it, and existing objects with no `clauses:` key keep their current
